Day 23: Listening for God’s Voice | Thursday of the Third Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
God is not silent —
but His voice is gentle.

Welcome to Day 23 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection invites you into the quiet, deeply needed practice of listening — not just hearing, not just noticing, but listening with a heart ready to receive.

Jesus says, “My sheep hear My voice.”  
Not because they are perfect,
but because they stay close to the Shepherd.

This spoken‑word devotional guides you into the stillness where God speaks:
through Scripture,
through silence,
through people,
and through the quiet movements of your heart.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why God’s voice is gentle, never forceful

How noise — external and internal — makes it hard to hear Him

Where God often speaks: Scripture, silence, love, and peace

A prayer to quiet your heart and open your ears

A simple daily activity: one minute of pure silence, just listening

If this reflection blesses you, consider continuing the journey through all 40 days of Lent.

Peace be with you.

